-- חוזר הממונה על השכר 2016-1-39 (23.8.2016) — קצובת נסיעה: החזר הוצאות נסיעה
-- בתחבורה ציבורית בעקבות הרפורמה בתחבורה הציבורית
-- How the public-sector employers pay the travel allowance after the
-- public-transport reform of 2016: who is paid under the reform's rules in
-- full, how existing employees who travel between cities are paid, the
-- Modiin / Beit Shemesh exception, the advances, moves of workplace or
-- home, the periodic declaration, and official travel at single-trip
-- tariffs.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `קצובת נסיעה - החזר הוצאות נסיעה בתחבורה ציבורית בעקבות הרפורמה בתחבורה הציבורית`

-- akn:preamble/p1 akn:preamble/p2 akn:preamble/p3 akn:preamble/p4 akn:preamble/p5 akn:preamble/p6 akn:preamble/p7 akn:preamble/p8 akn:preamble/p9 The letterhead (State of Israel, Ministry of Finance, Wage and Labour Agreements, its address), the date (23.8.2016), the circular's number, the addressees (the public-sector employers) and the subject line; no rule.

-- akn:preamble/p10 The reference line: the Ministry of Finance Director-General's letter of 10.7.2016 to the Histadrut, the outline this circular carries out; no rule of its own.

-- The reform as the circular recites it (the Accountant-General's takam
-- notice 13.4.2.1, editions 8 and 9): changes from 1.1.2016, a 14.5% cut in
-- the tariffs from 1.2.2016, and a further phase covering every locality
-- from 1.4.2016. Facts the rules below rest on, kept as data.
@ref akn:preamble/p11
`the reform's changes take effect` MEANS Date 1 1 2016

@ref akn:preamble/p11
`the reform's tariff cut` MEANS 14.5%

@ref akn:preamble/p11
`the tariff cut takes effect` MEANS Date 1 2 2016

@ref akn:preamble/p11
`the reform's further phase takes effect` MEANS Date 1 4 2016

-- akn:preamble/p12 The purpose: after talks between the Ministry of Finance and the Histadrut an outline was decided to limit the harm to the allowance of employees who travel between cities; no rule of its own.

-- akn:preamble/p13 "The instructions passed to the government ministries follow": an introduction to sections 1-3; no rule.

DECLARE `travel-allowance party` IS ONE OF
    `the public-sector employer`
    `the travelling employee`
    `the Accountant-General`

@desc An employee who claims the travel allowance, as far as this circular asks about it.
DECLARE `traveller` HAS
    `day hired by the current employer`                         IS A DATE    @desc the day the employee was taken on by the employer they work for now
    `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS A BOOLEAN @desc received an urban "חודשי חופשי" (code 614 in the State service) up to 31.12.2015
    `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS A BOOLEAN @desc received a travel allowance for intercity travel (codes 604 or 960 in the State service) up to 31.12.2015, on an individual basis for the days they actually came to work
    `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS A BOOLEAN @desc moved to another workplace of the same employer (another city or another government ministry) or changed residence, after the reform
    `travels between cities to work`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc travels to work by intercity lines now
    `moved from another employer`                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc came to the current employer from another employer
    `days actually worked in the month`                         IS A NUMBER  @desc the days the employee came to work in the month (reported as code 4820 in the State service)

-- An existing employee is one taken on by the current employer before
-- 1.1.2016 (§1א's own definition, repeated in §2's heading).
@ref akn:art_1__para_a akn:art_2
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an existing employee` t IF
    t's `day hired by the current employer` LESS THAN Date 1 1 2016

§§ `1 מקבלי קצובת נסיעה עליהם יחולו כללי הרפורמה במלואה`

DECLARE `travel-allowance rule` IS ONE OF
    `the urban monthly free pass at the reform's updated tariffs`
    `the reform's rules and tariffs`
    `a single-trip intercity tariff for each day actually worked`
    `a daily free pass for each day actually worked`
    `no intercity travel paid`
    `a rule the circular does not give`

-- §1א: existing employees who had an urban monthly pass up to 31.12.2015
-- get it at the reform's updated tariffs, paid automatically by postcode.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid the updated urban monthly pass under §1א` t IF
        `an existing employee` t
    AND t's `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`

-- §1ב: an employee taken on from 1.1.2016 is paid under the reform's rules
-- and tariffs, automatically by postcode.
@ref akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid under the reform's rules as a new employee under §1ב` t IF
    NOT `an existing employee` t

-- §1 heading: the reform's rules apply in full to the two groups that
-- follow, 1א and 1ב.
@ref akn:art_1
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reform's rules apply in full under §1` t IF
        `paid the updated urban monthly pass under §1א` t
    OR  `paid under the reform's rules as a new employee under §1ב` t

-- §§1א-1ב: both are paid automatically, by postcode, without a claim.
@ref akn:art_1__para_a akn:art_1__para_b
GIVEN r IS A `travel-allowance rule`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid automatically by postcode` r IF
    CONSIDER r
    WHEN `the urban monthly free pass at the reform's updated tariffs` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the reform's rules and tariffs` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `2 עובדים קיימים הנוסעים בנסיעות בינעירוניות`

-- §2א: an existing employee paid individually for intercity days up to
-- 31.12.2015 gets the single-trip tariff (at the reform's tariffs) times the
-- days actually worked.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid single intercity trips under §2א` t IF
        `an existing employee` t
    AND t's `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015`
    AND t's `travels between cities to work`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-a: "תעריף נסיעה בודדת כפול ימי
-- עבודה בפועל" pays, as written, ONE single-trip fare for each day; the
-- Director-General's letter it carries out pays single trips "(הלוך ושוב)",
-- there and back. The reading adopted is the letter's: two fares a day.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
`single-trip fares for each day worked as the circular writes it` MEANS 1

@ref akn:art_2__para_a
`single-trip fares for each day worked as read` MEANS 2

@desc The tariffs §2א's monthly amount is built from, all at the reform's tariffs and set outside this circular.
DECLARE `intercity tariffs` HAS
    `monthly free pass where the employee lives` IS A NUMBER @desc the urban monthly pass in the city of residence
    `monthly free pass where the employee works` IS A NUMBER @desc the urban monthly pass in the city of work
    `single intercity trip fare`                 IS A NUMBER @desc one single-trip fare between the two cities

-- §2א's own example: an employee from Tel Aviv working in Jerusalem gets the
-- Tel Aviv monthly pass, plus the Jerusalem-Tel Aviv intercity trips times
-- the days actually worked, plus the Jerusalem monthly pass.
@ref akn:art_2__para_a
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`, p IS A `intercity tariffs`, `fares a day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly allowance under §2א` t p `fares a day` IS
    p's `monthly free pass where the employee lives`
    PLUS (p's `single intercity trip fare` TIMES `fares a day` TIMES t's `days actually worked in the month`)
    PLUS p's `monthly free pass where the employee works`

-- §2ב: existing employees living in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and working in
-- Jerusalem get, "as an exception", a daily free pass for each day actually
-- worked. The exception takes them out of §2א.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid a daily free pass under §2ב` t IF
        `an existing employee` t
    AND t's `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`

-- §2ב's cost of a daily free pass, by the day it is for. The "(בקוד להשלים)"
-- after the first amount is a drafting note the published circular left
-- in ("code to be completed"): the payroll code was never filled in. It
-- names no rule and changes no amount.
@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the cost of a daily free pass` `the day` IS
    BRANCH IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 2 2016 THEN 26.5
           IF `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 1 2016 THEN 31
           OTHERWISE 0

@ref akn:art_2__para_b
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the monthly allowance under §2ב` t `the day` IS
    `the cost of a daily free pass` `the day` TIMES t's `days actually worked in the month`

-- §2ג: the advances paid to intercity travellers are cancelled
-- retroactively, from January 2016, for anyone whose allowance report is
-- corrected. (§2ד's deduction runs "from April 2016": the circular does not
-- say from when the advances were paid, so the two months are kept as
-- printed.)
@ref akn:art_2__para_c
`the advances are cancelled from` MEANS Date 1 1 2016

@ref akn:art_2__para_c
GIVEN `the allowance report was corrected` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the advances are cancelled` `the allowance report was corrected` IF
    `the allowance report was corrected`

@ref akn:art_2__para_d
`the retroactive deduction runs from` MEANS Date 1 4 2016

DECLARE `travel-allowance action` IS ONE OF
    `deduct the advances in the payslip`
    `sign the periodic declaration that the refund reflects the expense`
    `update the takam instruction`

-- §2ד: the retroactive deduction of the advances is made in the payslip
-- only where there is a report for paying the corrected allowance,
-- differences included. The text sets no time limit.
@ref akn:art_2__para_d
GIVEN `a corrected report with differences exists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `travel-allowance party` `travel-allowance action`
DECIDE `deducting the advances` `a corrected report with differences exists` IS
    IF `a corrected report with differences exists`
    THEN PARTY `the public-sector employer`
         MAY   `deduct the advances in the payslip`
    ELSE PARTY `the public-sector employer`
         SHANT `deduct the advances in the payslip`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the public-sector employer` BECAUSE "§2ד: the advances may be deducted only where the corrected allowance, differences included, is reported for payment"

-- §2ה: an existing employee who moves workplace within the same employer
-- (another city, another ministry) or moves home keeps the rules that
-- applied on the eve of the reform, at updated tariffs, intercity travel
-- included at single-trip tariffs times days actually worked.
@ref akn:art_2__para_e
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeps the pre-reform rules after a move under §2ה` t IF
        `an existing employee` t
    AND t's `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`

-- §2ו: such an employee who moved far and began travelling between cities
-- begins to be paid single-trip tariffs times days actually worked.
@ref akn:art_2__para_f
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `begins single intercity trips after a move under §2ו` t IF
        `keeps the pre-reform rules after a move under §2ה` t
    AND t's `travels between cities to work`

-- §2ז: one who moved near and stopped travelling between cities is paid no
-- intercity travel; everything follows the new address or workplace.
@ref akn:art_2__para_g
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `stops intercity travel after a move under §2ז` t IF
        `keeps the pre-reform rules after a move under §2ה` t
    AND NOT t's `travels between cities to work`

-- §2ח: one who moved from employer to employer is treated as a new
-- employee, under the reform's rules. F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-c: the words take in a move made
-- at any time, including before 1.1.2016, which §1א's definition makes an
-- existing employee; the reading adopted is a move on or after 1.1.2016 (the
-- letter's "שיעבור", "who will move"), where §2ח and the definition agree.
@ref akn:art_2__para_h
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as written` t IF
    t's `moved from another employer`

@ref akn:art_2__para_h
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as read` t IF
        t's `moved from another employer`
    AND t's `day hired by the current employer` AT LEAST `the reform's changes take effect`

-- The rule that applies, as the circular writes it. The order is the
-- circular's priorities: a new employee (§1ב, §2ח) first; §2ב's exception
-- before §2א; a move (§§2ה-2ז) before the pre-reform position; then §2א and
-- §1א. An existing employee in none of them is a case the circular does not
-- decide (F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-b).
-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-e: a Modiin or Beit Shemesh
-- resident who moved is in both §2ב and §2ו, and the text does not rank
-- them. Reading adopted: §2ב first, its "כחריג" read as the exception for
-- every existing resident it names, a mover included.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A `travel-allowance rule`
DECIDE `the rule the circular writes` t IS
    BRANCH IF `paid under the reform's rules as a new employee under §1ב` t          THEN `the reform's rules and tariffs`
           IF `treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as written` t           THEN `the reform's rules and tariffs`
           IF `paid a daily free pass under §2ב` t                                   THEN `a daily free pass for each day actually worked`
           IF `begins single intercity trips after a move under §2ו` t               THEN `a single-trip intercity tariff for each day actually worked`
           IF `stops intercity travel after a move under §2ז` t AND t's `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015`
                                                                                        THEN `no intercity travel paid`
           IF `paid single intercity trips under §2א` t                              THEN `a single-trip intercity tariff for each day actually worked`
           IF `paid the updated urban monthly pass under §1א` t                      THEN `the urban monthly free pass at the reform's updated tariffs`
           OTHERWISE `a rule the circular does not give`

-- The rule under the readings adopted (F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-b, F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-c): §2ח only for a move on
-- or after 1.1.2016; an existing employee the circular leaves out gets the
-- urban monthly pass at updated tariffs, as the letter's §1א gives every
-- existing employee by the accepted rules.
@export default The travel-allowance rule that applies to a public-sector employee under Wage Controller circular 2016-1-39 (the 2016 public-transport reform)
GIVEN t IS A `traveller` @desc the employee
GIVETH A `travel-allowance rule`
DECIDE `the travel-allowance rule` t IS
    CONSIDER `the rule the circular writes` (`the traveller as §2ח is read` t)
    WHEN `a rule the circular does not give` THEN `the urban monthly free pass at the reform's updated tariffs`
    OTHERWISE `the rule the circular writes` (`the traveller as §2ח is read` t)

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-c's reading first: an
-- employee who came from another employer before 1.1.2016 is taken as
-- not having moved employer, and F-…-b's reading then applies to them too.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A `traveller`
DECIDE `the traveller as §2ח is read` t IS
    IF      `treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as written` t
        AND (NOT `treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as read` t)
    THEN `as not having moved employer` t
    ELSE t

GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A `traveller`
DECIDE `as not having moved employer` t IS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS t's `day hired by the current employer`
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS t's `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS t's `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015`
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS t's `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS t's `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS t's `travels between cities to work`
        `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS t's `days actually worked in the month`

-- §2ט: existing employees who travel between cities and are paid under the
-- above must sign a periodic declaration that the refund reflects the
-- expense. The circular sets no period; time is in months, and the period
-- is an input. F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-d: the letter conditions EVERY existing employee's
-- payment on the declaration, not only the intercity travellers'.
@ref akn:art_2__para_i
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must sign the periodic declaration under §2ט` t IF
        `an existing employee` t
    AND t's `travels between cities to work`
    AND (   `the travel-allowance rule` t EQUALS `a single-trip intercity tariff for each day actually worked`
         OR `the travel-allowance rule` t EQUALS `a daily free pass for each day actually worked`)

@ref akn:art_2__para_i
GIVEN `the declaration period` IS A NUMBER @desc the period, in months, for which one declaration is given; the circular says only "periodic"
GIVETH A DEONTIC `travel-allowance party` `travel-allowance action`
DECIDE `the periodic declaration` `the declaration period` IS
    PARTY `the travelling employee`
    MUST  `sign the periodic declaration that the refund reflects the expense`
    WITHIN `the declaration period`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the travelling employee` BECAUSE "§2ט: an existing intercity traveller must sign a periodic declaration that the refund reflects the expense"

-- §2י: the Accountant-General's takam instruction will be updated
-- accordingly. No date is given, so the duty has no time limit.
@ref akn:art_2__para_j
GIVETH A DEONTIC `travel-allowance party` `travel-allowance action`
DECIDE `updating the takam instruction` IS
    PARTY `the Accountant-General`
    MUST  `update the takam instruction`

§§ `3 נסיעות בתפקיד בתעריפי תחבורה ציבורית`

@desc An official trip by public transport, as far as section 3 asks about it.
DECLARE `official trip` HAS
    `the employee has a service car and is past the kilometre quota` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the employee has no car entitlement`                            IS A BOOLEAN @desc no "תקן רכב"
    `outside the city`                                               IS A BOOLEAN @desc the trip leaves the city, including a trip inside the regional monthly free-pass zone that is not inside the city

-- §3, for existing and new employees alike: an employee with a service car
-- travelling beyond the kilometre quota, or with no car entitlement, is
-- paid for official public-transport trips outside the city, including
-- inside the regional monthly free-pass zone (not within the city), at
-- single-trip tariffs.
@ref akn:art_3/p1
GIVEN o IS AN `official trip`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an official trip paid at single-trip tariffs` o IF
        (o's `the employee has a service car and is past the kilometre quota` OR o's `the employee has no car entitlement`)
    AND o's `outside the city`

-- akn:art_3/p2 A link to the Ministry of Transport's site, which shows the metropolitan maps and computes a fare by rings from origin to destination; a tool, no rule.

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off (Yossi Cohen, acting Wage Controller), the copy to the Civil Service Commissioner, the circular's serial (2016-106) and the distributor's address; no rule.

§§ `Findings`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-a: one fare a day as written, two (there and back) as read: the
-- monthly allowance differs.
`a Tel Aviv commuter to Jerusalem` MEANS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 9 2010
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS TRUE
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS TRUE
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS FALSE
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS TRUE
        `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 20

-- Placeholder tariffs, round figures; the reform's tariffs are not in this circular.
`placeholder tariffs` MEANS
    `intercity tariffs` WITH
        `monthly free pass where the employee lives` IS 200
        `monthly free pass where the employee works` IS 200
        `single intercity trip fare`                 IS 20

`one fare a day as written and a return as read give different allowances` MEANS
    NOT (`the monthly allowance under §2א` `a Tel Aviv commuter to Jerusalem` `placeholder tariffs` `single-trip fares for each day worked as the circular writes it`
         EQUALS `the monthly allowance under §2א` `a Tel Aviv commuter to Jerusalem` `placeholder tariffs` `single-trip fares for each day worked as read`)
#ASSERT `one fare a day as written and a return as read give different allowances`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-b: an existing employee who had neither an urban monthly pass nor an
-- individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015, lives outside Modiin and
-- Beit Shemesh and has not moved, is in no clause.
`an existing employee with no pre-reform allowance` MEANS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 3 2014
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS FALSE
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS FALSE
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS FALSE
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS FALSE
        `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 21

`an existing employee without a pre-reform allowance is in no clause` MEANS
    `the rule the circular writes` `an existing employee with no pre-reform allowance` EQUALS `a rule the circular does not give`
#ASSERT `an existing employee without a pre-reform allowance is in no clause`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-c: an employee who came from another employer in 2014 is an existing
-- employee by §1א's definition and a new one by §2ח's words.
`an employee who changed employer in 2014` MEANS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 6 2014
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS TRUE
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS TRUE
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS FALSE
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS TRUE
        `moved from another employer`                               IS TRUE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 20

`a pre-reform change of employer is both existing and new` MEANS
        `an existing employee` `an employee who changed employer in 2014`
    AND `treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as written` `an employee who changed employer in 2014`
    AND NOT (`the rule the circular writes` `an employee who changed employer in 2014`
             EQUALS `the rule the circular writes` (`as not having moved employer` `an employee who changed employer in 2014`))
#ASSERT `a pre-reform change of employer is both existing and new`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-d: an existing employee on the urban pass alone signs nothing under
-- §2ט; the letter conditions that employee's payment on the declaration too.
`an existing employee on the urban pass alone` MEANS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 9 2012
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS TRUE
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS FALSE
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS FALSE
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS FALSE
        `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 21

`an existing urban-pass employee is not required to declare` MEANS
        `an existing employee` `an existing employee on the urban pass alone`
    AND NOT `must sign the periodic declaration under §2ט` `an existing employee on the urban pass alone`
#ASSERT `an existing urban-pass employee is not required to declare`

§§ `Examples`

#ASSERT `the travel-allowance rule` `a Tel Aviv commuter to Jerusalem` EQUALS `a single-trip intercity tariff for each day actually worked`
#ASSERT `must sign the periodic declaration under §2ט` `a Tel Aviv commuter to Jerusalem`

-- §2א's example with placeholder tariffs, a return each day as read:
-- 200 + 20 × 2 × 20 + 200.
#ASSERT `the monthly allowance under §2א` `a Tel Aviv commuter to Jerusalem` `placeholder tariffs` `single-trip fares for each day worked as read` EQUALS 1200

#ASSERT `the travel-allowance rule` `an existing employee with no pre-reform allowance` EQUALS `the urban monthly free pass at the reform's updated tariffs`
#ASSERT `the travel-allowance rule` `an employee who changed employer in 2014` EQUALS `a single-trip intercity tariff for each day actually worked`
#ASSERT `paid automatically by postcode` (`the travel-allowance rule` `an existing employee on the urban pass alone`)

`a new employee hired in March 2016` MEANS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 3 2016
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS FALSE
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS FALSE
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS TRUE
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS TRUE
        `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 20

-- §2ב is for EXISTING employees: a new Modiin resident is under the reform.
#ASSERT `the travel-allowance rule` `a new employee hired in March 2016` EQUALS `the reform's rules and tariffs`

`a Modiin resident working in Jerusalem` MEANS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 9 2008
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS TRUE
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS TRUE
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS TRUE
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS TRUE
        `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 20

#ASSERT `the travel-allowance rule` `a Modiin resident working in Jerusalem` EQUALS `a daily free pass for each day actually worked`
#ASSERT `the monthly allowance under §2ב` `a Modiin resident working in Jerusalem` (Date 15 1 2016) EQUALS 620
#ASSERT `the monthly allowance under §2ב` `a Modiin resident working in Jerusalem` (Date 15 3 2016) EQUALS 530

-- The daily pass's two costs agree with the reform's 14.5% cut (31 less
-- 14.5% is 26.505), to the half-shekel the circular prints.
#ASSERT (`the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 1 1 2016) TIMES (1 MINUS `the reform's tariff cut`)) MINUS `the cost of a daily free pass` `the tariff cut takes effect` LESS THAN 0.01

`a Tel Aviv commuter who moved home near Jerusalem` MEANS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 9 2010
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS TRUE
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS TRUE
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS FALSE
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS TRUE
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS FALSE
        `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 20

#ASSERT `the travel-allowance rule` `a Tel Aviv commuter who moved home near Jerusalem` EQUALS `no intercity travel paid`

`an official trip outside the city without a car entitlement` MEANS
    `official trip` WITH
        `the employee has a service car and is past the kilometre quota` IS FALSE
        `the employee has no car entitlement`                            IS TRUE
        `outside the city`                                               IS TRUE
#ASSERT `an official trip paid at single-trip tariffs` `an official trip outside the city without a car entitlement`

-- §2ד on a timeline in months: deducting without a corrected report is a
-- breach; with one, the deduction is permitted.
#TRACE `deducting the advances` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the public-sector employer` DOES `deduct the advances in the payslip` AT 1
#TRACE `deducting the advances` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the public-sector employer` DOES `deduct the advances in the payslip` AT 1
#TRACE `the periodic declaration` 12 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the travelling employee` DOES `sign the periodic declaration that the refund reflects the expense` AT 2

§§ `Property checks`

-- The circular's rules over their whole finite space: every traveller
-- hired on 31.12.2015 or on 1.1.2016 with each of the seven yes-or-no
-- facts, kept to the travellers the facts allow (a Modiin or Beit Shemesh
-- resident working in Jerusalem travels between cities, and so does one
-- paid for intercity days to 31.12.2015 who has not moved since); 0 to 23
-- days worked and one or two fares a day; the days the circular names and
-- the day before each; and every official trip.

`both booleans` MEANS LIST TRUE, FALSE
`the hiring days checked` MEANS LIST Date 31 12 2015, Date 1 1 2016

GIVEN h IS A DATE, u IS A BOOLEAN, i IS A BOOLEAN, m IS A BOOLEAN, v IS A BOOLEAN, x IS A BOOLEAN, e IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `traveller`
DECIDE `a checked traveller` h u i m v x e IS
    `traveller` WITH
        `day hired by the current employer`                         IS h
        `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS u
        `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS i
        `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS m
        `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS v
        `travels between cities to work`                            IS x
        `moved from another employer`                               IS e
        `days actually worked in the month`                         IS 20

GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the facts allow` t IF
        ((NOT t's `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`) OR t's `travels between cities to work`)
    AND ((NOT t's `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015`)
         OR t's `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`
         OR t's `travels between cities to work`)

GIVEN p IS A FUNCTION FROM `traveller` TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds for every traveller the facts allow` p IF
    all (GIVEN h YIELD
            all (GIVEN u YIELD
                    all (GIVEN i YIELD
                            all (GIVEN m YIELD
                                    all (GIVEN v YIELD
                                            all (GIVEN x YIELD
                                                    all (GIVEN e YIELD
                                                            (NOT `the facts allow` (`a checked traveller` h u i m v x e))
                                                            OR p (`a checked traveller` h u i m v x e))
                                                        `both booleans`)
                                                `both booleans`)
                                        `both booleans`)
                                `both booleans`)
                        `both booleans`)
                `both booleans`)
        `the hiring days checked`

GIVEN p IS A FUNCTION FROM `traveller` TO BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds for some traveller the facts allow` p IF
    NOT `holds for every traveller the facts allow` (GIVEN t YIELD NOT p t)

-- §1א, §1ב: an employee is existing exactly when hired before 1.1.2016;
-- no one is both §1א's and §1ב's; and §1 takes in exactly the existing
-- holders of an urban pass and every new employee.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 1 sorts the employee once` t IF
        `an existing employee` t EQUALS (t's `day hired by the current employer` LESS THAN Date 1 1 2016)
    AND NOT (`paid the updated urban monthly pass under §1א` t AND `paid under the reform's rules as a new employee under §1ב` t)
    AND `the reform's rules apply in full under §1` t
        EQUALS ((`an existing employee` t AND t's `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`) OR NOT `an existing employee` t)
#ASSERT `holds for every traveller the facts allow` `section 1 sorts the employee once`

-- Under the readings adopted, every traveller has a rule; a new employee
-- has the reform's; §2ט asks a declaration only of an existing intercity
-- traveller.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adopted rule decides every traveller` t IF
        NOT (`the travel-allowance rule` t EQUALS `a rule the circular does not give`)
    AND ((`an existing employee` t) OR `the travel-allowance rule` t EQUALS `the reform's rules and tariffs`)
    AND ((NOT `must sign the periodic declaration under §2ט` t)
         OR (`an existing employee` t AND t's `travels between cities to work`))
#ASSERT `holds for every traveller the facts allow` `the adopted rule decides every traveller`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-b over the whole space: the
-- rule the circular writes is missing exactly for an existing employee
-- who came from no other employer, had neither an urban pass nor an
-- intercity allowance to 31.12.2015, is not a Modiin or Beit Shemesh
-- resident, and is not a mover now travelling between cities.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the circular gives no rule exactly to an existing employee with no pre-reform allowance` t IF
    (`the rule the circular writes` t EQUALS `a rule the circular does not give`)
    EQUALS (    `an existing employee` t
            AND NOT t's `moved from another employer`
            AND NOT t's `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`
            AND NOT t's `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015`
            AND NOT t's `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`
            AND NOT (t's `moved workplace within the employer or moved home` AND t's `travels between cities to work`))
#ASSERT `holds for every traveller the facts allow` `the circular gives no rule exactly to an existing employee with no pre-reform allowance`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-c over the whole space: §2ח
-- as written and as read part exactly for an existing employee who came
-- from another employer.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§2ח's readings part exactly for an existing employee from another employer` t IF
    (NOT (`treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as written` t EQUALS `treated as new after moving employer under §2ח as read` t))
    EQUALS (`an existing employee` t AND t's `moved from another employer`)
#ASSERT `holds for every traveller the facts allow` `§2ח's readings part exactly for an existing employee from another employer`

-- §2ב and §§2ה-2ו: the clauses an existing employee can fall under at
-- once, and the rule each gives on its own. §2ב's "כחריג" makes it the
-- exception to §2א; nothing in the text ranks it against a move.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§2ב and §2ו both apply` t IF
        `paid a daily free pass under §2ב` t
    AND `begins single intercity trips after a move under §2ו` t

-- They meet exactly for an existing Modiin or Beit Shemesh resident
-- working in Jerusalem who moved home or workplace.
GIVEN t IS A `traveller`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `§2ב and §2ו meet exactly for a Modiin or Beit Shemesh resident who moved` t IF
    `§2ב and §2ו both apply` t
    EQUALS (    `an existing employee` t
            AND t's `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`
            AND t's `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`)
#ASSERT `holds for every traveller the facts allow` `§2ב and §2ו meet exactly for a Modiin or Beit Shemesh resident who moved`

-- F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-e: there is such an
-- employee, and the two clauses give them different rules — a daily free
-- pass for each day worked, or a single-trip fare for each day worked. A
-- Jerusalem employee on the urban pass who moved home to Modiin in 2016:
`a Jerusalem employee who moved home to Modiin` MEANS
    `a checked traveller` (Date 31 12 2015) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE

`§2ב and §2ו both apply and give different rules` MEANS
        `holds for some traveller the facts allow` `§2ב and §2ו both apply`
    AND `§2ב and §2ו both apply` `a Jerusalem employee who moved home to Modiin`
    AND NOT (`a daily free pass for each day actually worked` EQUALS `a single-trip intercity tariff for each day actually worked`)
    AND `the travel-allowance rule` `a Jerusalem employee who moved home to Modiin` EQUALS `a daily free pass for each day actually worked`
#ASSERT `§2ב and §2ו both apply and give different rules`

-- §2א over 0 to 23 days worked and one or two fares a day, on the
-- placeholder tariffs: never below the two monthly passes, never falling
-- with more days; F-2016-08-23_sachar_2016-1-39_nesia-reform-a over the
-- whole space: a return each day pays more than one fare exactly on a day
-- worked.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN d YIELD
                LET t MEANS `traveller` WITH
                                `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 9 2010
                                `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS TRUE
                                `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS TRUE
                                `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS FALSE
                                `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
                                `travels between cities to work`                            IS TRUE
                                `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
                                `days actually worked in the month`                         IS d
                    s MEANS `traveller` WITH
                                `day hired by the current employer`                         IS Date 1 9 2010
                                `received the urban monthly free pass up to 31.12.2015`     IS TRUE
                                `received an individual intercity allowance up to 31.12.2015` IS TRUE
                                `lives in Modiin or Beit Shemesh and works in Jerusalem`    IS FALSE
                                `moved workplace within the employer or moved home`         IS FALSE
                                `travels between cities to work`                            IS TRUE
                                `moved from another employer`                               IS FALSE
                                `days actually worked in the month`                         IS d PLUS 1
                IN  all (GIVEN f YIELD
                                `the monthly allowance under §2א` t `placeholder tariffs` f AT LEAST 400
                            AND `the monthly allowance under §2א` t `placeholder tariffs` f AT MOST `the monthly allowance under §2א` s `placeholder tariffs` f)
                        (LIST `single-trip fares for each day worked as the circular writes it`, `single-trip fares for each day worked as read`)
                    AND (`the monthly allowance under §2א` t `placeholder tariffs` `single-trip fares for each day worked as read`
                         GREATER THAN `the monthly allowance under §2א` t `placeholder tariffs` `single-trip fares for each day worked as the circular writes it`)
                        EQUALS (d GREATER THAN 0))
            (range 0 23)

-- §2ב's daily pass by day: nothing before 1.1.2016, 31 from that day, 26.5
-- from 1.2.2016 and not the day before; it never rises.
`the daily pass steps on the days §2ב names` MEANS
        `the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 31 12 2015) EQUALS 0
    AND `the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 1 1 2016) EQUALS 31
    AND `the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 31 1 2016) EQUALS 31
    AND `the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 1 2 2016) EQUALS 26.5
    AND `the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 1 2 2016) LESS THAN `the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 31 1 2016)
    AND `the cost of a daily free pass` (Date 31 12 2016) EQUALS 26.5
#ASSERT `the daily pass steps on the days §2ב names`

-- §1א: an employee hired on 31.12.2015 is existing, one hired on 1.1.2016
-- is new, and §2ג's retroactive cancellation runs from the reform's day.
`existing and new meet at 1.1.2016` MEANS
        `an existing employee` (`a checked traveller` (Date 31 12 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
    AND NOT `an existing employee` (`a checked traveller` (Date 1 1 2016) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
    AND `the advances are cancelled from` EQUALS `the reform's changes take effect`
#ASSERT `existing and new meet at 1.1.2016`

-- §3 over every official trip: paid at single-trip tariffs exactly outside
-- the city, for an employee past a service car's quota or with no car
-- entitlement.
#ASSERT all (GIVEN q YIELD
                all (GIVEN n YIELD
                        all (GIVEN o YIELD
                                `an official trip paid at single-trip tariffs`
                                    (`official trip` WITH `the employee has a service car and is past the kilometre quota` IS q, `the employee has no car entitlement` IS n, `outside the city` IS o)
                                EQUALS ((q OR n) AND o))
                            `both booleans`)
                    `both booleans`)
            `both booleans`
